*******************************************************************************	Filename: 	.uacrc *	Author:		P. Enlund 3/10/94*	Key bindings for UAC_view are the same syntax as .umacsrc except we can *	define different key bindings for the different TERM types which we might *	find ourselves supporting.*	Consequently this file will not have to be changed when we change terminal*	or use more than one terminal type on the same login path. *   This file is searched for in 3 places in the following order*	1)	./uacrc					( nice for testing here !)*	2)  /dd/sys/.uacrc*	3)  /h0/sys/.uacrc**	The first one found is used if none found UAC_view uses it's default*	cursor key settings. The keys listed below are the only definable keys*	*   UAC_view prints error messages relating to this file before using defaults*	******************************************************************************* Section referenced if TERM=wy50 #if TERM w1bind-to-key	next-line				^J				* Cntrl Jbind-to-key	previous-line			^K				* Cntrl Kbind-to-key page-up					M-J				* Esc Jbind-to-key page-down				M-K				* Esc Kbind-to-key cursor-home				^~				* Cntrl tildasbind-to-key cursor-end				M-{				* Esc {bind-to-key back-space		       ^H				* Cntrl H#endif*** Section for TERM=vt100 #if TERM vt100bind-to-key	next-line               M-[Bbind-to-key	previous-line           M-[Abind-to-key page-up					M-[Ebind-to-key page-down				M-2Jbind-to-key cursor-home				M-[Hbind-to-key cursor-end				M-[Kbind-to-key back-space		       ^H				* Cntrl H#endif** ******************************************************************************